  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Outbox pattern via River",
      "items": [
        "the user write and its email must commit together — River's river.AddTx delivers the outbox pattern with no outbox table, no claim CTE, no leases",
        "enqueues ride riverClient.AddTx(ctx, args) with Tx: the SAME Postgres transaction as the sqlc write — at-least-once by construction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Fetch + work",
      "items": [
        "River workers pull durable river_job rows — at-least-once, deduped by UniqueOpts; no poll interval, batch size or SKIP LOCKED CTE to tune",
        "the worker calls Work(ctx, job): render + send via the sender port — Console in dev, SMTP in prod; migrations ran with golang-migrate as a deploy step, never startup"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Failure + purge",
      "items": [
        "errors follow River's backoff and discard after the configured max attempts — visible in river_job and in slog rows, not in email_jobs",
        "river.PeriodicJobs (cron spec) covers the old janitor sweep: expired sessions, email_verifications and password_resets purged hourly; audit rows and rotation history untouched"
      ]
    }
  ]
